==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leǵ-}}
From {{der|en|frm|collectif}}, from {{der|en|la|collēctīvus}}, from {{m|la|collēctus}}, past participle of {{m|la|colligō|t=I collect}}, from {{m|la|com-|t=together}} + {{m|la|legō|t=I gather}}. Compare {{cog|fr|collectif}}. {{doublet|en|colectivo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈlɛktɪv/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-collective.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|col|lec|tive|caption=Hyphenation, US}}; {{hyphenation|en|col|lect|ive|caption=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛktɪv|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Formed by gathering or collecting; gathered into a mass, sum, or body.
#: {{syn|en|congregated|aggregated}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''collective''' body of a nation}}
# Tending to [[collect]]; forming a [[collection]].
#* {{RQ:Young Night-Thoughts|18|night=4|Local is his throne {{...}} to fix a point, / A central point, '''collective''' of his sons.}}
# Having [[plurality]] of origin or authority.
# {{lb|en|grammar}} Expressing a collection or aggregate of [[individual]]s, by a singular form.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Deducing consequences; [[reasoning]]; [[inferring]].
#* {{RQ:Browne Religio Medici|passage=critical and '''collective''' reason}}

