===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[farm]] owned by a [[collection]] of people.
# {{lb|en|especially|in communist countries}} One of more [[farm]]s managed and owned, through the state, by the [[community]].
# {{lb|en|grammar}} A [[collective noun]] or name.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[group]] dedicated to a particular [[cause]] or [[interest]].
#* '''2005''', Zoya Kocur, Simon Leung, ''Theory in contemporary art since 1985'' (page 76)
#*: There are, however, a number of contemporary artists and art '''collectives''' that have defined their practice precisely around the facilitation of dialogue among diverse communities.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Holland Cotter|title=The Collective Conscious|work=The New York Times|date=2006-03-05|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2006/03/05/arts/design/the-collective-conscious.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Critical Art Ensemble is one of many art '''collectives''' operating on the principle that information is power and that it is most effectively made available through a combination of science and aesthetics.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Adam Bradley|title=The Creative Collectives Finding Strength in Numbers|work=The New York Times|date=2021-10-13|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/10/13/t-magazine/black-art-collectives-creators.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Today’s '''collectives''' create together, tour together, exhibit together, live together, survive together, eat together, sleep together, march together, fight together and party together, too.}}

